# Linear Status Sync

Every roadmap change maps to a Linear issue (project **NextSlope MVP**, team **10xNextSlope**).
Always reflect real progress in Linear — update status at these transitions, then tell the user
which issue moved and to what state.

## When to update (use the `linear` MCP `save_issue` tool)

| Trigger | Move issue to |
|---|---|
| Starting work on a change (first phase begins) | **In Progress** |
| Whole branch finished — final review before merge to `main` (PR open) | **In Review** |
| Change finished / archived via `/10x-archive` | **Done** |

**In Review is the final review gate only.** Enter it once the *entire* change branch is complete
(all phases done) and is up for its final pre-merge review on the PR to `main` — never during
intermediate phase work. While phases are still being implemented, the issue stays **In Progress**.

## How

- Find the issue by its Roadmap ID / Change ID (e.g. search "S-01" or `account-authentication`).
  The issue description carries both `Roadmap ID:` and `Change ID:`.
- Read `mcps/plugin-linear-linear/tools/save_issue.json` for the schema before calling.
- If no matching issue exists, tell the user rather than guessing or creating one unprompted.
- If the issue is already in the target state, do nothing (don't churn status).

## Discipline

- Update status as a side effect of the work actually happening — not in advance. Move to
  In Progress when you genuinely start, to Done only after the change is archived.
- A status change in Linear is a claim about reality; never mark Done a change whose final PR
  to `main` has not merged.
